# User Deletion Protection Walkthrough

## Goal
Prevent the deletion of users who are assigned key roles (Executive, Deputy) within the organization structure, ensuring business integrity.

## Implementation

### 1. Custom Exception
Created `App\Exceptions\CannotDeleteKeyUserException` to handle the error logic for both JSON (API) and Web requests.

```php
// app/Exceptions/CannotDeleteKeyUserException.php
class CannotDeleteKeyUserException extends Exception
{
    public function render(Request $request): JsonResponse|RedirectResponse
    {
        $message = 'You cannot delete a user holding a key role (e.g., Executive, Deputy).';
        // ... handles 422 JSON or Redirect back with errors
    }
}
```

### 2. Protection Logic in Model
Added [isProtectable()](file:///Users/s-a-c/Herd/chrrprr/app/Models/User.php#91-107) method to [User](file:///Users/s-a-c/Herd/chrrprr/app/Models/User.php#19-108) model. This uses a direct database query to ensure it finds role assignments regardless of Eloquent scopes or caching, and checks the database directly.

```php
// app/Models/User.php
public function isProtectable(): bool
{
    $pivotTable = config('permission.table_names.model_has_roles');
    // ... direct DB join query to check for restricted roles
}
```

### 3. Trait for Event Precedence
Created `App\Models\Concerns\ProtectsKeyRoles` trait to register the [deleting](file:///Users/s-a-c/Herd/chrrprr/app/Observers/UserObserver.php#12-22) event listener.
**Crucial:** This trait must be used *before* Spatie's [HasRoles](file:///Users/s-a-c/Herd/chrrprr/vendor/spatie/laravel-permission/src/Traits/HasRoles.php#21-37) trait in the [User](file:///Users/s-a-c/Herd/chrrprr/app/Models/User.php#19-108) model. This ensures our protection logic runs **before** Spatie detaches the roles!

```php
// app/Models/Concerns/ProtectsKeyRoles.php
trait ProtectsKeyRoles
{
    public static function bootProtectsKeyRoles(): void
    {
        static::deleting(function ($user) {
            if ($user->isProtectable()) {
                throw new CannotDeleteKeyUserException();
            }
        });
    }
}
```

### 4. User Model Integration
Updated [User](file:///Users/s-a-c/Herd/chrrprr/app/Models/User.php#19-108) model to use the trait in the correct order.

```php
// app/Models/User.php
class User extends Authenticatable
{
    use ProtectsKeyRoles; // <--- REGISTERED FIRST = RUNS FIRST
    use HasRoles; 
    // ...
}
```

## Verification
`UserDeletionConstraintTest` passes all checks:
- [x] Cannot delete a user who is an executive
- [x] Cannot delete a user who is a deputy
- [x] Can delete a user after roles are removed

The test expects [CannotDeleteKeyUserException](file:///Users/s-a-c/Herd/chrrprr/app/Exceptions/CannotDeleteKeyUserException.php#10-42) which is now correctly thrown.
